{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1547938-weird-question-about-the-5-maidens-does-one-of-them-die-off-each-new-age","id":1547938,"title":"Weird question about the 5 Maidens - does one of them die off each new age?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-24T13:42:40-08:00","id":1547938,"title":"Weird question about the 5 Maidens - does one of them die off each new age?","content":"I don't remember where I heard or read this but I remember something weird like one of the 5 Maidens dies every time a new age starts in Creation and is thus replaced; was this a) ever an actual thing? b) If it was what edition and book was it from? c) If it was a thing, did each new maiden have the same theme as the last one or a new theme (for example, if Mercury died, would the new Maiden by the Maiden of Journeys or a Maiden of something like Stories, Beginnings or Faults)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T03:52:25-08:00","id":1548019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1547938-weird-question-about-the-5-maidens-does-one-of-them-die-off-each-new-age#post1547938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember where I heard or read this but I remember something weird like one of the 5 Maidens dies every time a new age starts in Creation and is thus replaced; was this a) ever an actual thing? b) If it was what edition and book was it from? c) If it was a thing, did each new maiden have the same theme as the last one or a new theme (for example, if Mercury died, would the new Maiden by the Maiden of Journeys or a Maiden of something like Stories, Beginnings or Faults)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have definitely read on something along those lines too, but no idea if it's an obscure bit of lore in the books or Ink Monkeys articles past or simply some very popular bit of fanon, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-03-2025, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T17:01:32-08:00","id":1548100,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is official in any way. It might have been some popular fanon somewhere (but if so, i must have completely missed it). I'm quite sure it's not in any official sources though (including Ink Monkeys stuff)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T15:59:23-08:00","id":1548312,"title":"","content":"It sounds like the kind of thing that the Manual book might have included as a throwaway reference among many. I regard that book as attempting to build a sense of mythos around the Maidens, but not really having a great idea of what form that should take or how to go about accomplishing it.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't a direct part of Oversight, it's at least something that could have been part of the book's tone from which Oversight arose.<br /> <br /> (That said, I would expect such a thing to be presented as rumour and legend rather than fact)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T08:34:47-08:00","id":1548472,"title":"","content":"I wonder to what extent it was writers trying to be cute about Saturn's original colour being orange, similar to how Yellow Jade could only be created by accident because it's original inclusion in the write-up for Slayer Khatars was a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-13-2025, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T07:39:33-08:00","id":1548516,"title":"","content":"According to other people I asked this is misremembering a part of the 2nd ed sidereal book that suggest (on page page 225):<br /> <br /> &quot;Or perhaps a new Maiden arises every so often to replace one of the Five. Each time this happens, a portion of the current Sidereals are lost or changed. Can the lost Sidereal Essences be recovered (perhaps from a hidden vault in the Orrery of Rathess)? What happens when the next Sixth Maiden comes into her own (and what might this mean for Nexus)?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T10:21:00-08:00","id":1548519,"title":"","content":"I remembered that but wasn't sure of it was the origin of the sixth maiden concept. <br /> <br /> The real question here is, do you think it's neat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T14:49:53-08:00","id":1548689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1547938-weird-question-about-the-5-maidens-does-one-of-them-die-off-each-new-age?p=1548519#post1548519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remembered that but wasn't sure of it was the origin of the sixth maiden concept.<br /> <br /> The real question here is, do you think it's neat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if I used if this <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Mnemosynis/MonkeyExalts\" target=\"_blank\">(unforunately undeveloped) fan splat idea</a> maybe, otherwise I don't quite see the point","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T18:51:45-07:00","id":1550368,"title":"","content":"I think this was among the potential plot seeds for the Emissary of Nexus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-28T04:27:49-07:00","id":1551325,"title":"","content":"Yep. Specifically, <b>The Unnamed Maiden:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;An Age is more than a historical demarcation marked arbitrarily on paper by some savants. It marks the end of the Tapestry of Fate, when the last spools of thread run dry and the pattern spiders sit idle, waiting for the Maiden who will sacrifice herself to form more thread. At the end of each Age, a Maiden dies and a new Maiden is born, waiting for her time and letting the world mark her, so that she may flavor the threads of the next era. That is what the Emissary is\u2014a goddess for an Age yet to come. She sits at the center of Nexus because she must. She nests at the center of activity and life in the world, drawing on all experience with wide eyes and silent lips. She watches, whispers and learns. In Nexus, she sees humanity at its purest, its most decadent, its most honest, and she learns what the next Age will bring. Behind her mask, her face holds the shape of the Third Age, already formed, waiting to be revealed. But not even she knows what it looks like, and she will know only when the spiders pull away her mask in those final moments before her destruction and the birth of her child.&quot; (<i>The Scavenger Lands</i>, Page 138)<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, not one of the Five Maidens everyone knows about, and not an entity most people are <i>ever</i> going to know about. In case you're curious, the other <i>four</i> options listed for the Emissary are:<br /> <br /> <b>The Last Solar: </b>Specifically, a surviving First Age Eclipse Caste Solar who hid outside of time until the Great Contagion unraveled his spell and kicked him back out into Creation. His mask hides from fate, but spending any peripheral essence would risk damaging his disguise and &quot;endanger his life to Sidereal hunters who remain as powerful as he once was.&quot;, though I'd phrase it more as attracting an unhealthy amount of attention from the Bronze Faction. Quite possibly the <i>entire</i> Bronze Faction. I mean, a <i>First Age Solar</i> who's been hiding out in Nexus and manipulating things from behind the scenes? Clearly <i>he's</i> the reason everything's going wrong!<br /> <br /> <b>The Resurrected Man: </b>Someone tried to do the impossible, to bring someone back from the dead, and as this was 2e and Liminals didn't exist yet, what they got instead was &quot;a puppet upon<br /> the fingers of a monstrous, undead god&quot;, a pawn of the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> <b>The Scam Artist:</b> The Emissary is just a figurehead for the Council of Nexus, being a mortal imbued with essence to become functionally God-Blooded; in the current setting, they could be an exigent.<br /> <br /> <b>The Inner Council:</b> It's a Sidereal, a Lunar, and a few other friends secretly working together.<br /> <br /> I wish more of 2e had been like this; more &quot;here are some options&quot; than &quot;here is the canon, which you must obey&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28792-beron-the-grey","name":"Beron the Grey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28792_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T10:44:57-07:00","id":1551429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beron the Grey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1547938-weird-question-about-the-5-maidens-does-one-of-them-die-off-each-new-age?p=1551325#post1551325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite possibly the <i>entire</i> Bronze Faction. I mean, a <i>First Age Solar</i> who's been hiding out in Nexus and manipulating things from behind the scenes? Clearly <i>he's</i> the reason everything's going wrong!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they're going to be that intimidated by a First Age Solar; they killed hundreds of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}